  "guidebook": {
    "intro": "Biashara ndogo huendesha Afrika Mashariki: vibanda, maduka, mafundi na mawakala wa pesa. Haya ni maneno ya biashara kwa Kiingereza.",
    "phrases": [
      { "target": "How is business going?", "base": "Biashara inaendaje?" },
      { "target": "We made a profit.", "base": "Tumepata faida." },
      { "target": "I put money aside every week.", "base": "Ninaweka akiba kila wiki." },
      { "target": "Show me your goods.", "base": "Nionyeshe bidhaa zako." },
      { "target": "Teach me, please.", "base": "Nifundishe, tafadhali." }
    ],
    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "how-going",
        "title": "How is it going?",
        "body": [
          "**Inaendaje?** ni **How is it going?** au **How’s business?** Majibu: **It’s going well**, **Not bad**, **It’s slow** (inaenda polepole).",
          "**Kupata faida** ni **make a profit**, si “get a profit”. **Kupata hasara** ni **make a loss**."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "make-let",
        "title": "Teach, show, give back",
        "body": [
          "**-isha/-esha** ya Kiswahili mara nyingi ni kitenzi kipya kwa Kiingereza: **-funda → teach**, **-ona → show**, **-rudi → give back**.",
          "Mtu huja baada ya kitenzi: **Teach me** (nifundishe), **Show me** (nionyeshe), **Give it back to me** (nirudishie)."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "Savings group",
        "body": ["**Chama** huitwa kwa Kiingereza **savings group**. Benki hutoa **a loan** (mkopo) na **interest** (riba)."]
      }
    ]
  },
